WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.370
Around four in five
people in India are Hindu,

2
00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.180
and Hindu festivals fill the calendar.

3
00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:13.580
Yet in 1976, India wrote a new word into
the opening of its Constitution: secular.

4
00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:18.290
In some countries, secular means a
wall between the state and religion.

5
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.940
So what does secular mean in India?

6
00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:25.530
In this mission, you'll compare three
ways a state can deal with religion.

7
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.630
Then you'll see how religion
in India is changing,

8
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.330
and judge whether India is
a genuinely secular state.

9
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:36.910
Your mission: find out what India
means when it calls itself secular.
